431
01:43:19.570 --> 01:43:21.570
He is talking about physical thirst.

432
01:43:25.570 --> 01:43:27.570
Those who drink this water here from that well,

433
01:43:28.570 --> 01:43:30.570
they will be thirsty again.

434
01:43:42.570 --> 01:43:47.570
But the water that I give will become in him a spring welling up to eternal life.

435
01:43:49.570 --> 01:43:50.570
What is He talking about here?

436
01:43:52.570 --> 01:43:53.570
Is this a metaphor?

437
01:43:53.570 --> 01:43:54.570
Is this a metaphor?

438
01:43:56.570 --> 01:43:57.570
Nice story in my Bible?

439
01:43:59.570 --> 01:44:00.570
Or is it real?

440
01:44:02.570 --> 01:44:03.570
Or do they say...

441
01:44:18.570 --> 01:44:21.570
When you eat and drink, you will become hungry and thirsty again.

442
01:44:23.570 --> 01:44:24.570
And that is what she says.

443
01:44:25.570 --> 01:44:26.570
The woman says, sir.

444
01:44:27.570 --> 01:44:28.570
She doesn't even know who he is.

445
01:44:29.570 --> 01:44:30.570
Sir, who are you?

446
01:44:33.570 --> 01:44:35.570
Give me this water so that I won't get thirsty.

447
01:44:36.570 --> 01:44:37.570
She is still thinking in the natural.

448
01:44:43.570 --> 01:44:44.570
It takes a lot to come to this water.

449
01:44:45.570 --> 01:44:46.570
