455
01:45:07.570 --> 01:45:08.570
You need me.

456
01:45:11.570 --> 01:45:12.570
You are at number 6.

457
01:45:13.570 --> 01:45:14.570
I am your number 7.

458
01:45:15.570 --> 01:45:16.570
You have arrived at number 6.

459
01:45:17.570 --> 01:45:18.570
I am your number 7.

460
01:45:33.570 --> 01:45:36.570
He is her seventh and true husband.

461
01:45:37.570 --> 01:45:39.570
He is the one who will give her that satisfaction.

462
01:45:44.570 --> 01:45:46.570
He met her as the seventh man.

463
01:45:53.570 --> 01:45:55.570
Jesus tells us how we should live.

464
01:45:56.570 --> 01:45:57.570
Okay, verse 27.

465
01:46:10.570 --> 01:46:14.570
From verse 27 we see that at that moment His disciples returned.

466
01:46:14.570 --> 01:46:17.570
And they were amazed that He was talking with a woman.

467
01:46:25.570 --> 01:46:26.570
And yet no one asked...

468
01:46:27.570 --> 01:46:29.570
What do you want with her or why are you speaking with her?

469
01:46:40.570 --> 01:46:43.570
And the woman left her jar and ran into the city.

470
01:46:43.570 --> 01:46:44.570
And she said to everyone...

471
01:46:45.570 --> 01:46:47.570
Come, see a man who told me everything I ever did.

472
01:46:47.570 --> 01:46:48.570
Could this be the Messiah?

473
01:46:56.570 --> 01:46:58.570
And she did not feel ashamed.

474
01:46:58.570 --> 01:47:01.570
She says, Jesus, He knows everything. He could very well be the Messiah.

475
01:47:05.570 --> 01:47:07.570
And the people went out of the city to Him.

476
01:47:14.570 --> 01:47:16.570
And meanwhile the disciples said to Jesus...

477
01:47:17.570 --> 01:47:18.570
Rabbi, you need to eat something.

478
01:47:26.570 --> 01:47:30.570
And it takes time to go into the city and come back.

479
01:47:30.570 --> 01:47:32.570
So I think that was a fixed day for Jesus.

480
01:47:32.570 --> 01:47:34.570
In which He was simply busy with His mission.

481
01:47:37.570 --> 01:47:39.570
He hasn't eaten anything for hours, in any case.

482
01:47:45.570 --> 01:47:46.570
And then He said...

483
01:47:47.570 --> 01:47:48.570
But He said to them...

484
01:47:49.570 --> 01:47:50.570
I have food to eat.

485
01:47:51.570 --> 01:47:53.570
That you disciples know nothing.

486
01:47:55.570 --> 01:47:56.570
But He said to them...

487
01:47:57.570 --> 01:47:58.570
I have food that you do not know about.

488
01:48:05.570 --> 01:48:06.570
And his disciples said...

489
01:48:06.570 --> 01:48:09.570
Could someone have brought Him something to eat?

490
01:48:14.570 --> 01:48:15.570
They think in the natural.

491
01:48:18.570 --> 01:48:20.570
They only think about that satisfaction in the natural.

492
01:48:25.570 --> 01:48:27.570
Have you ever been in worship for so long...

493
01:48:27.570 --> 01:48:30.570
that you might have been hungry, but you weren't even aware of it?

494
01:48:38.570 --> 01:48:41.570
When you come in here last night, perhaps still hungry in your stomach...

495
01:48:41.570 --> 01:48:43.570
during that worship you don't notice it at all.

496
01:48:44.570 --> 01:48:45.570
You don't feel it.

497
01:48:46.570 --> 01:48:47.570
Because you are focused.

